    class PolymorphicOffsetPtrAllocator <<utility>> {
        - memory_resource_proxy_ : OffsetPtr<MemoryResourceProxy>
        --
        + Allocate(n) : OffsetPtr<T>
        + Deallocate(p, n) : void
    }

    note right of PolymorphicOffsetPtrAllocator
        The PolymorphicOffsetPtrAllocator must store an OffsetPtr to the 
        MemoryResourceProxy because it does a bounds check to ensure that
        it's pointing to the correct memory resource (i.e. the one in which)
        it's currently residing. This must be done in the proxy because the 
        bounds checking algorithm relies on the MemoryResourceProxy residing
        in the same resource that it's pointing to. A PolymorphicOffsetPtrAllocator 
        can be allocated outside the memory region (e.g. on the stack) so can't 
        do the check itself.
    end note
}

