note right of MappedRegionFactory
    In order to mock the MappedRegionFactory, we would need it to be a singleton (and 
    dispatch either to a mock or to the real implementation). In order to avoid having 
    a singleton but be able to mock the MappedRegionFactory, we would need to have the user
    create and store an instance of the MappedRegionFactory themselves instead of the MemoryRegionRegistry.
    This makes sense because the registry cannot exist without the factory. So rather than passing the 
    registry to factory calls, the registry would instead be owned by the factory instance.

    The MappedRegionFactory owns the IMappedRegionRegistry since the registry makes no sense
    without a factory (because without the factory, there are no resources and then the registry
    would be empty anyway).

    The MappedRegionFactory is a friend of all MappedRegions and 
    can access their private constructors to create instances.

    We don't enforce (via singleton pattern, aou etc.) that only one MappedRegionFactory (and 
    therefore MappedRegionRegistry) can exist per process. We will just add a note in the docs of
    the class that if the same shm resource is opened by multiple factories, it will remap the same
    region in the process. The reasons for this are:
        - We want to avoid a singleton pattern due to static initialization order issues.
        - If a user wants to use MappedRegionFactory in multiple places (e.g. within mw/com and in 
        another place), we would need to add public apis to hand down references the the single 
        instance in the process.
        - These different parts of the code path should also not be opening the same resources. So
        it makes sense that they do not see the resources of the other factory / registry.

    If the InitializationCallback fails (i.e. return an error), then we should remove we created
    region from the registry (even if it's the persistent registry). The registry should only hold
    valid and initialized regions. 
end note

interface IMappedRegion <<interface>> {
    ' Constructor should have documentation explaining that the derived class need to 
    ' take optional<InitializationCallback> as a constructor argument.
    + IMappedRegion(optional<InitializationCallback>)

    ' GetId() should not change after calling AdjustToProperties. 
    + AdjustToProperties(IMappedRegionProperties&) : Result<void>
    + GetBaseAddress() : void*
    + GetSize() : size_t
    + GetProperties() : IMappedRegionProperties&
    + GetId() : IMapIdType
}

note left of IMappedRegion
    The GetId() method returns a unique identifier for the memory region 
    which depends on the specific memory type. E.g. a named region might 
    create the id by hashing the path name, an anonymous region might 
    use the anonymous handle id etc. It will be stored in the MemoryResourceProxy
    and used to identify the memory region within the SharedMemoryResourceRegistry.

    The specific implementation of IMappedRegion needs to handle synchronization between
    different processes / threads trying to create / open the same region.
end note

